DEVLOG — updates.txt seventh pass (4f56230)

/more is now 1504px, from 2798px two passes ago (~2.9 -> 1.6 screens), with
nothing removed. The saving came from PAIRING short blocks into shared rows
and from making the stats a detail line instead of a section, not from
cutting content.

DRIFT WALL was picked over option-wheel and infinite-spiral because it is the
only one of the three that keeps all 12 items visible; the other two show one
at a time, which contradicts "without cutting out information altogether".
Its perf rule: pointer movement writes exactly TWO custom properties on the
wall inside a rAF, and each tile derives its transform from those by depth.
Do not set a transform per tile per pointer event — that is what makes walls
like this stutter.

FLOWING MENU now has a "columns" prop: 0 = original full-width rows,
>0 = grid of cells with identical hover/marquee/entry-direction behaviour.
Added so the countries could stay compact AND keep the effect.

BEAMS: the user reported them glossing the photo/quote. They were NOT — the
photo column is z-40, rays z-30, verified by cropping the figure. Six
overlapping narrow shafts were brightening the whole hero, which reads the
same way. Fewer + wider blades fixed the perception. Check the actual
stacking before changing z-index in response to a glare report.

TRAVEL descriptions are still placeholders the user will rewrite himself;
they surface only in the hover marquee, so editing more.ts touches no markup.

STILL OPEN: "later we'll add more stuff and content on the more page".
Leadership was left roomy for that.
